// fsht-data crash regression (user report: pinContextTo segfault on an
// I/O heavy program): semaProgram's struct-field binding loop used a
// range-for over p->structs while binding a field type APPENDS to
// p->structs (the String prelude is created on demand; Vec<u8> /
// Result<..> instantiate) — a push_back past capacity reallocates
// the vector and the cached iterators walk FREED memory, crashing
// inside pinContextTo.  Exactly 256 records (a power-of-two
// capacity boundary) make the first mid-loop prelude push the 257th
// entry — a deterministic realloc on the pre-fix build.
struct R0 { name: String, tag: i64 }
struct R1 { bytes: Vec<u8>, n: i64 }
struct R2 { r: Result<u8, IoError>, k: i64 }
